WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.870
- [Instructor] What we're going to do

00:00:00.870 --> 00:00:02.010
in this video is think about how

00:00:02.010 --> 00:00:05.790
we might multiply 592 times seven.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.490
And in general we're gonna think about

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:09.210
how we would approach
multiplying something

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.610
that has multiple digits times something

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.170
that has one digit.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.690
And the way we're going
to do it is the way

00:00:14.690 --> 00:00:15.890
that, if you were to ask your parents,

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:17.690
it's probably the way that they do it.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.040
And so the typical approach is

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.230
you would write the larger
multi digit number on top

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:25.880
and then you would write the
smaller single digit number

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.140
below that, and since
it's in the ones place,

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:30.580
the seven, you would put it
in the ones place column.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:31.971
So you'd put it right below the ones place

00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:35.390
in the larger number,
so right below that two.

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.070
And then you'd write the
multiplication symbol.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:39.620
And the way you'd think about it is,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:41.930
all right, I'm just gonna
take each of these places

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:43.760
and multiply it by the seven.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.500
So, for example, if I'm
taking those two ones

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:49.130
and I'm multiplying it times seven,

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.060
well that's gonna be 14 ones.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:52.880
Well there's no digit for 14.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:55.150
I can only put four of
those ones over here.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.940
And then the other 10 ones I can express

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.960
as one 10, and so I'd put it up there.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.150
Sometimes when people learn it,

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:03.836
they say, hey, two times seven is 14.

00:01:03.836 --> 00:01:06.520
I write the four and I carry the one.

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:07.620
But all you're doing is you're saying,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.910
hey, 14 is one 10 plus four ones.

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:14.011
But then you move over to the tens place.

00:01:14.011 --> 00:01:17.400
You say, hey, what's
nine tens times seven?

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.010
Well, nine times seven is 63,

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:23.730
so nine tens times seven is 63 tens,

00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:26.280
plus another 10 is 64 tens.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:28.374
You can only put four
of those tens over here.

00:01:28.374 --> 00:01:33.374
So the other 60 tens you
can express as six hundreds,

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:34.860
so you can stick that right over there.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.930
Now a lot of people would
explain that as saying,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:40.850
hey, nine times seven
is 63, plus one is 64.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.670
Write the four and carry the six.

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.730
But hopefully you understand
what we mean by carrying.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.644
You're really trying to write 64 tens.

00:01:47.644 --> 00:01:50.600
Only four of those tens
can be expressed over here.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.200
Or that's maybe the cleanest way to do it.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:55.770
And then the other 60 tens you
can express as six hundreds.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.820
And then, last but not least,

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.820
five hundreds times seven
is going to be 35 hundreds,

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:08.690
and then you add six
hundreds, you get 41 hundreds.

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:13.690
So 41 hundreds, so it's 4,144.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:16.174
Now I wanna reconcile this, or connect it,

00:02:16.174 --> 00:02:19.810
to with other ways that
you might have seen this.

00:02:19.810 --> 00:02:22.390
So let's say that, let's do this again.

00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:27.363
So if we were to write 592 times seven.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.300
So one way that we've
approached it in the past is

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.290
we say, all right, what's two times seven?

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.570
Well that's going to be 14.

00:02:35.570 --> 00:02:37.250
Notice that's the same 14.

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.960
We're just representing it
a little bit differently.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.150
Then we might say, well
what is nine times seven?

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.763
Gonna do the same color.

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.960
And this really nine tens times seven.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.100
That's 63 tens, so you might
write it right over there,

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.420
which is the same thing as 630.

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.200
And then you could think about

00:02:57.200 --> 00:03:00.330
what is five hundreds times seven?

00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:03.780
Well that's 35 hundreds, so
you could write it like that.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:08.780
Same thing as 3500, and then
you would add everything up.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.530
So you have a total of four ones.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:14.060
You have a total of four tens.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:16.150
You have a total of 11 hundreds.

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.700
You could right 100 there.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.720
And then regroup the other 10 hundreds

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.047
into the thousands place as 1000.

00:03:23.047 --> 00:03:26.370
1000 plus three thousands is 4000.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:27.920
So we got the exact same answer because

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:29.205
we essentially did the same thing.

00:03:29.205 --> 00:03:32.260
Over here, when we were carrying it,

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:34.530
we were essentially
regrouping things from here

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.290
and you could think about
it where we're condensing

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.920
our writing versus what we did here.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.400
Here we just very systematically
said two times seven,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.709
nine times seven, five times seven,

00:03:42.709 --> 00:03:45.160
but we made sure to
keep track of the places

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:46.195
to figure out what each of those,

00:03:46.195 --> 00:03:49.300
you could think of it as
partial products, would be,

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:50.460
and then we added.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.370
While here we carried along the way,

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:54.270
essentially regrouping
the values when we said,

00:03:54.270 --> 00:03:56.480
hey, two ones times seven ones,

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.520
that's 14 ones, which is the same thing

00:03:58.520 --> 00:04:01.790
as four ones plus one 10.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:03.050
And so on, and so forth.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:05.740
So I encourage you, one, it's
good to learn this method.

00:04:05.740 --> 00:04:09.090
It's the most common
way that folks multiply.

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:11.690
Once again, your parents
probably learned it this way,

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.022
but it's really valuable to understand

00:04:13.022 --> 00:04:15.280
why these two things are the same thing,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:16.510
so really ponder that.

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.470
Think about that.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.270
And see if you can, if it all makes sense

00:04:20.270 --> 00:04:21.103
what's going on there.

00:04:21.103 --> 00:04:23.943
You're not just blindly
memorizing the steps.

